&lt;h2&gt;In a nutshell&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we continue building the best milkman on earth, we’re looking for frontend engineers who want to shape the digital shopping experience used by millions across Europe. We’re looking for people with experience in B2C product companies at scale, where engineering quality, customer impact, and product thinking are essential. You’ll thrive in our international environment, where clear communication and close collaboration across product, design, backend, analytics, and frontend teams are crucial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is not a role where you simply receive tickets and implement predefined solutions. You will help shape the problem, challenge assumptions, make technical decisions, and work with others to create the best experience for our customers.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, in addition to working with React daily you&#39;ll be working with our powerful server-driven UI framework that&#39;s at the heart of our business&#39;s success:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Powers our entire shopping app and enables rapid iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives sophisticated personalization at scale, delivering tailored content to each user&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empowers our business teams to operate the store autonomously - dozens of operators and analysts make every day real-time updates without any further tech involvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you can expect to work with a wide range of technologies within the JavaScript ecosystem, across the full stack! Experience with React Native is not required, we’ll get you up to speed with that on the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build for millions:&lt;/strong&gt; Work in a small, collaborative team to build and evolve Picnic’s consumer-facing Store and Web experiences across mobile and web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn problems into products:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate customer and business needs into clear technical plans, practical frontend solutions, and shipped features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape decisions together:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with product, design, backend, analytics, and frontend colleagues while clearly communicating your reasoning and making trade-offs visible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively improve code quality, performance, processes, and team practices beyond your immediate responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable Picnic to move faster:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to our server-driven UI and shared frontend architecture, while owning your work from understanding the problem through feedback and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional software development experience, with strong frontend experience in React, React Native, TypeScript, or a similar JavaScript framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping and maintaining customer-facing applications, with a strong focus on testing and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product-minded approach: able to turn ambiguous customer or business problems into clear technical plans and thoughtful trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, structured communicator who collaborates effectively with product, design, backend, analytics, and frontend teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive owner who improves things beyond their assigned work, shares their perspective, adapts to new information, and remains eager to learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine motivation to build consumer and e-commerce experiences used by millions, with willingness to work from&lt;strong&gt; Picnic’s Amsterdam office-first environment&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✍🏼 Every expert was once a beginner!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including the Picnic Tech Academy, Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training. We also offer free professional weekly language courses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🫱🏼‍🫲🏾 Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍎 You are what you eat&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get freshly prepared, healthy lunches and snacks (with plenty of vegetarian, vegan, and halal options). Coffee snob? Don’t worry, our amazing Picnic barista has you covered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚴🏽 Stay healthy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials. There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga, to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔋 Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self, as well as 25 vacation days per year, so you can recharge your batteries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌍 Benefits for expats&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It can be daunting starting a new job AND moving to a new country. That’s why we offer lots of support for our many expat colleagues, if you want to find our relocation benefits, see &lt;a href=&quot;https://jobs.picnic.app/en/relocation&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As we continue to expand our operations, we are seeking a passionate and experienced Fruit and Vegetable Operations Lead. You will safeguard product taste and quality from field to fork, turning quality into a primary driver for our growth. Together, we will set the standard for a scalable, high-performance operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us in our mission to deliver the highest quality products and redefine the grocery shopping experience for our customers!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;In a nutshell&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Fruit and Vegetable Operations Lead, you will play a vital role in ensuring that our customers consistently receive top-quality fruit and vegetables. Your responsibilities will include implementing and maintaining rigorous quality control procedures throughout our fruit and vegetable supply chain, from sourcing to delivery. This role requires a keen attention to detail, strong communication skills, leadership skills and a deep understanding of industry-standard quality benchmarks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality performance management:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor and evaluate the performance of our products suppliers, providing feedback and guidance as needed to improve quality and consistency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality control: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct regular inspections of products to assess freshness, quality, and compliance with specifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a fruit and vegetable expert: &lt;/strong&gt;Stay informed about industry trends, developments, and emerging technologies related to product quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process implementation: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop and implement Picnic&#39;s quality control processes for vegetables and fruits, including product specifications, inspection criteria and quality assurance across our warehouses and Fulfilment Centres.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Train and educate Picnic&#39;s quality team members on quality control procedures, product specifications, and best practices for handling and storing products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplier management: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with Picnic&#39;s suppliers to establish and maintain quality standards, resolve quality issues, and ensure compliance with food safety regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder management: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams at Picnic, including buying, category management, and customer service, to address quality-related issues and implement corrective actions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of experience in a leadership role within a grocery / retail environment with knowledge of fruit and vegetables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong knowledge of produce quality standards, grading systems, and industry best practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attention to detail, with the ability to identify and address quality issues effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designs and executes comprehensive quality strategies while driving alignment across stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment and manage multiple priorities simultaneously.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication and relationship management skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willingness to travel in the Netherlands, occasionally France &amp;amp; Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fluent in English, Dutch fluency is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Picnic perks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Every expert was once a beginner!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including the Picnic Tech Academy, Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training. We also offer free professional weekly language courses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll work in an awesome scale-up environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay healthy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials. There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to equal opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Picnic is an equal opportunity employer—this means that all decisions regarding applications will be based on qualifications and merit. Applicants will be regarded independently of age, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, ethnicity, skin color, civil status, religious beliefs, physical or mental disability, or any other factors protected by law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic, we celebrate and value our differences and are committed to building a safe and inclusive working environment where everyone can be themselves.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Application&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate across the Netherlands with sites in Utrecht, Eindhoven, Rotterdam, Heerenveen, Zwolle, Nijmegen, and Geldermalsen. We are always looking for top talent to strengthen our operations team. If you want to join Picnic but don&#39;t see an open Site Lead vacancy in your preferred location, please submit an open application here to join our talent pool. Our recruiting team regularly reviews candidates in this pipeline and will reach out as soon as a matching role opens up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As FC Lead, your mission is to build a high-performance, customer-first culture by enabling your team and creating a great place to work. You own site performance across safety, quality, and cost, with an driving excellence through 6S standards and Lean programs. By prioritizing leadership coaching and internal team development you deliver sustainable, reliable results that consistently exceed customer expectations.​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the site:&lt;/strong&gt; Take responsibility for site performance on a weekly, period, and annual basis, meeting safety, quality, and operational KPIs.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build people culture:&lt;/strong&gt; Create a high-performance environment where teams are supported, motivated, and accountable.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop leaders:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide and coach Operations Managers and Supervisors to strengthen leadership quality across the site.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive key metrics:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver results on retention, perfect deliveries, delivery capacity, UPH, cost, and operational standards.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage incidents and planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Handle critical incidents, manage escalations, and ensure smooth operational planning and continuity.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead HR and external affairs:&lt;/strong&gt; Primary contact for the FC People Partner with direct accountability for complex HR cases; work with external stakeholders and authorities as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in relevant field​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years operations experience, including large multi-shift teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead, coach, and build high-performing teams​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving Lean and continuous improvement initiatives​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to deliver results through KPIs and operational standards​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills, managing critical incidents ​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English and Dutch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location Flexible:&lt;/strong&gt; We have sites throughout the Netherlands in the following locations; Utrecht, Eindhoven, Rotterdam, Heerenveen, Zwolle, Nijmegen, and Geldermalsen. During your application we will consider together which site makes most sense for you to begin your journey at Picnic. We are a fast-paced, growing company and due to this we require location flexibility from our Operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll receive a competitive compensation package, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 vacation days per year to recharge your batteries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The option to lease a car&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll get freshly prepared, healthy breakfast, lunches (and dinner at the FC) as well as delicious snacks and drinks available at all Picnic locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible company pension plan called “Doenpensioen” at a.s.r.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Picnic laptop and smartphone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An awesome scale-up atmosphere with the freedom to drive your own projects and the opportunity to have an impact!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to work in an international environment with motivated team members &amp;amp; legendary company events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many internal learning and development possibilities as well as professional soft skill &amp;amp; leadership trainings at a specialized external party&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

