&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master&#39;s degree &lt;/strong&gt;in HR, Psychology, Business, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 to 5 years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; as an HR Advisor, HR Business Partner, or similar role in a fast-paced environment (experience partnering with tech/engineering teams is a strong plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent communication skills&lt;/strong&gt; and a proven ability to work effectively with cross-functional tech stakeholders across multiple levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven project management and operations experience&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;8,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driven to challenge convention&lt;/strong&gt;, ask &quot;How can we do this better?&quot;, and reinvent how work is done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;8,5,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A natural ability to coach&lt;/strong&gt;, support, and develop technical teams and leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;8,6,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to see the big picture&lt;/strong&gt; while applying a clear, data-driven approach to complex people problems.&lt;/li&gt;
